Read the byte-compare words in GetMatch with memcpy instead of a type-punned dereference

GetMatch() compares the input eight bytes at a time by casting two unaligned
`unsigned char*` to `size_t*` and dereferencing them. That is undefined
behaviour (misaligned access) and upstream has an open report of it faulting
on strict-alignment hardware (google/zopfli#22, SIGBUS on MIPS64). With GCC
16 at the -O3 CMake uses for Release builds the loop is now vectorised on
x86_64 with aligned loads (movdqa + pcmpeqq), because the size_t* cast lets
the optimiser assume 8-byte alignment, and `zopfli` segfaults in
ZopfliFindLongestMatch on ordinary input (a 500-line text file). aarch64 is
unaffected only because NEON loads tolerate misalignment.

memcpy into a local word is the defined way to express the same read; the
compiler still folds it into a single (unaligned) load, so the 8-bytes-at-a-
time fast path is kept.

Upstream: https://github.com/google/zopfli/issues/22 (open, no fix on master
as of zopfli-1.0.3 / 2026-09).

--- a/src/zopfli/lz77.c	2026-09-30 09:52:39.262001829 -0500
+++ b/src/zopfli/lz77.c	2026-09-30 09:52:39.262910392 -0500
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
 
 void ZopfliInitLZ77Store(const unsigned char* data, ZopfliLZ77Store* store) {
   store->size = 0;
@@ -300,15 +301,26 @@
                                      const unsigned char* safe_end) {
 
   if (sizeof(size_t) == 8) {
-    /* 8 checks at once per array bounds check (size_t is 64-bit). */
-    while (scan < safe_end && *((size_t*)scan) == *((size_t*)match)) {
+    /* 8 checks at once per array bounds check (size_t is 64-bit). The two
+       pointers are byte pointers with no alignment guarantee, so read them
+       with memcpy (which the compiler turns into unaligned loads) instead of
+       dereferencing a cast, which lets the optimizer assume size_t alignment
+       and emit aligned vector loads that fault on misaligned input. */
+    size_t a, b;
+    while (scan < safe_end) {
+      memcpy(&a, scan, sizeof(a));
+      memcpy(&b, match, sizeof(b));
+      if (a != b) break;
       scan += 8;
       match += 8;
     }
   } else if (sizeof(unsigned int) == 4) {
     /* 4 checks at once per array bounds check (unsigned int is 32-bit). */
-    while (scan < safe_end
-        && *((unsigned int*)scan) == *((unsigned int*)match)) {
+    unsigned int a, b;
+    while (scan < safe_end) {
+      memcpy(&a, scan, sizeof(a));
+      memcpy(&b, match, sizeof(b));
+      if (a != b) break;
       scan += 4;
       match += 4;
     }
